<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henan is a province of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> on the middle and lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhengzhou">Zhengzhou</a> as its capital. Often called the cradle of Chinese civilisation, it holds the Erlitou site, the Shang capitals at Zhengzhou and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anyang">Anyang</a>, and the old imperial capitals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a>. Many states of the Zhou period lay within it, and it remains one of China's most populous provinces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henan.jpg" alt="Henan" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shang_Inscribed_Ox_Scapula_(for_divination).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
